WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.216
The school respiratory sequence builds on Week One assessment. Its purpose is to connect what you see with the physiological problem, choose support and discover promptly whether that support works.
学校呼吸教学承接第一周评估，目的是把观察与生理问题连接起来、选择支持，并及时判断支持是否有效。

00:00:12.216 --> 00:00:25.752
A patient can have an open airway but inadequate ventilation, or adequate ventilation but poor oxygen transfer. Naming the failing function is more useful than simply announcing a breathing problem.
患者可能气道通畅却通气不足，也可能通气足够但氧交换不良。指出失效功能，比只说“呼吸问题”更有用。

00:00:25.752 --> 00:00:37.056
Start with immediate threats and obtain help early. Do not postpone opening an obstructed airway or assisting inadequate breathing while completing an extensive respiratory history.
先处理即时威胁并及早求援。不能为完成详细呼吸病史，推迟开放阻塞气道或辅助不足呼吸。

00:00:37.056 --> 00:00:52.056
This lecture follows all seven school sections, including the treatment-failure loop. The separate airway-device lesson develops insertion and suction techniques; memorizing a device name is not a substitute for these functional decisions.
本讲覆盖学校七个部分，包括治疗失败后的循环。另一气道器械课展开置入及吸引技术；记住器械名称不能替代这些功能判断。

00:00:52.056 --> 00:01:06.240
The upper route conducts and conditions air. Loss of tone can let soft tissues obstruct the pharynx; swelling or foreign material can obstruct a different level. A visible mouth does not prove a patent route to the lungs.
上方通路传导及调节空气。张力丧失可使软组织阻塞咽部，肿胀或异物可阻塞其他层面。看得见口腔，不等于到肺的全程通畅。

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:20.376
The tracheobronchial tree distributes gas. Smooth-muscle narrowing, swelling and secretions increase resistance, particularly in smaller airways. The work required to move the same gas volume rises.
气管支气管树分配气体。平滑肌收缩、肿胀及分泌物增加阻力，小气道尤其明显，推动同样气量需要更多功。

00:01:20.376 --> 00:01:32.232
Alveoli provide a thin exchange surface beside flowing capillary blood. Ventilation must reach that surface and perfusion must reach the same region for effective gas exchange.
肺泡在流动毛细血管血液旁提供薄交换面。通气和灌注必须到达相同区域，气体交换才有效。

00:01:32.232 --> 00:01:45.696
The pump can fail even when the airway is open: depressed drive, muscle fatigue, weakness or a disrupted chest can reduce effective breaths. Examine the whole route and pump, not only breath sounds.
即使气道开放，呼吸泵仍会失效：驱动受抑、肌疲劳、无力或胸部破坏可使有效呼吸减少。应检查整个通路及泵，而非只听诊。

00:01:45.696 --> 00:02:00.384
During ordinary inspiration, diaphragm contraction increases thoracic volume and lowers alveolar pressure below atmospheric pressure. Air moves down the resulting pressure gradient, not because the lungs actively suck on their own.
普通吸气时膈肌收缩增大胸腔容积，使肺泡压低于大气压。空气沿压差移动，不是肺本身主动吸气。

00:02:00.384 --> 00:02:14.592
At rest, expiration largely follows elastic recoil. Obstructed airways can need longer to empty; another forced breath before exhalation finishes can trap gas and increase intrathoracic pressure.
静息呼气主要依靠弹性回缩。阻塞气道可能需更久排空；尚未呼完又强行送气，可造成气体潴留及胸内压增加。

00:02:14.592 --> 00:02:29.928
Resistance concerns opposition to airflow. Compliance concerns volume change for a pressure change. A stiff, poorly compliant lung and a narrowed airway can both be hard to ventilate, but they are not the same mechanism.
阻力指对气流的阻碍；顺应性指单位压力变化引起的容积变化。僵硬低顺应性肺与狭窄气道都难通气，但机制不同。

00:02:29.928 --> 00:02:44.208
Positive-pressure support can improve ventilation or recruitment but may reduce venous return. Greater bag force is not automatically better oxygen delivery, especially in shock or dynamic hyperinflation.
正压支持可改善通气或复张，但可能减少静脉回流。更用力挤球不自动改善氧输送，尤其在休克或动态过度充气时。

00:02:44.208 --> 00:02:59.088
Use a simplified adult teaching example with an assumed dead-space volume of zero point one five litres per breath. These numbers illustrate a relationship; they are not a patient-specific measurement or a prescribed tidal volume.
用简化成人教学例，假定每次死腔零点一五升。这些数字仅说明关系，不是患者实测值或规定潮气量。

00:02:59.088 --> 00:03:13.320
At twenty breaths of half a litre, minute ventilation is ten litres and estimated alveolar ventilation is seven litres per minute. The portion remaining in conducting dead space does not exchange gas in the same way.
每分钟二十次、每次半升，分钟通气量十升，估算肺泡通气量七升。留在传导死腔的部分，不同样参与气体交换。

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:27.840
At forty quarter-litre breaths, minute ventilation is still ten litres, but estimated alveolar ventilation falls to four litres. A high rate cannot be interpreted without the depth and effectiveness of each breath.
每分钟四十次、每次四分之一升，分钟通气量仍为十升，但估算肺泡通气降至四升。高频率必须结合每次深度及有效性解释。

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:44.352
This explains why respiratory rate alone can falsely reassure. Observe chest movement, air entry, effort, mental state and the carbon-dioxide trend; do not calculate a normal-looking minute volume from guessed bedside volumes.
这解释了只看频率为何可能误判。应观察胸廓运动、进气、用力、意识及二氧化碳趋势，不要拿床旁猜测容积算出“正常”分钟通气量。

00:03:44.352 --> 00:03:57.864
A person sitting forward and speaking in short phrases is giving functional information before the stethoscope is applied. Observe work of breathing and the ability to sustain it, not just the displayed oxygen saturation.
前倾坐位、只能说短句的患者，在听诊前已提供功能信息。应观察呼吸功及能否持续，不只看显示血氧。

00:03:57.864 --> 00:04:13.752
Compare both sides and several appropriate chest locations on skin. Note air entry, added sounds and any asymmetry. Clothing, a noisy vehicle and an incomplete examination must be recognized as limitations.
在皮肤上比较双侧及多个适当胸部位置，注意进气、附加音及不对称。衣物、车内噪声和不完整检查都是需承认的局限。

00:04:13.752 --> 00:04:31.152
Ask about sudden versus gradual onset, chest discomfort, fever, cough, swelling, exposures, trauma and prior episodes. Confirm actual inhaler or oxygen use rather than inferring a diagnosis from equipment beside the patient.
询问突发还是渐起、胸部不适、发热、咳嗽、肿胀、暴露、创伤及既往发作。核实吸入器或氧疗实际使用，不凭旁边设备推断诊断。

00:04:31.152 --> 00:04:45.816
Use a baseline and repeat the relevant findings after intervention. If ventilation is immediately inadequate, treatment and a concise assessment occur together; the full history can follow without abandoning reassessment.
建立基线，干预后重查相关发现。通气已不足时，应并行治疗及简要评估；随后再补病史，同时持续复评。

00:04:45.816 --> 00:05:01.536
Respiratory distress describes increased difficulty and effort. Failure means the respiratory system cannot adequately perform its oxygenation or ventilation task. The two can overlap, and failure does not always look dramatic.
呼吸窘迫指困难及用力增加；衰竭指系统无法充分完成氧合或通气任务。两者可重叠，衰竭不一定外观激烈。

00:05:01.536 --> 00:05:16.632
A severely distressed patient who becomes quiet, sleepy and shallow may be exhausting rather than recovering. A rate falling from thirty-four to ten is not good news if chest expansion and responsiveness also decline.
严重窘迫者转为安静、嗜睡和浅呼吸，可能是耗竭而非恢复。频率从三十四降至十，若胸廓扩张及反应也下降，并非好消息。

00:05:16.632 --> 00:05:32.112
Sedatives or opioids can suppress drive without an earlier period of marked effort. Examine airway integrity, breath depth and the circulation; a normal saturation on oxygen can coexist with dangerous carbon-dioxide retention.
镇静药或阿片可直接抑制驱动，不一定先经历明显费力。检查气道完整性、深度及循环；吸氧时血氧正常仍可能存在危险二氧化碳潴留。

00:05:32.112 --> 00:05:45.120
Escalate support and resources when function fails. Do not leave an inadequately ventilating patient on CPAP simply because the mask was already fitted or its saturation initially improved.
功能失败时应升级支持及资源。不能因已戴上 CPAP 或起初血氧改善，就让通气不足者继续留在该治疗上。

00:05:45.120 --> 00:06:00.840
The school oxygen cascade moves from available environmental oxygen to cellular use. Treat it as a causal map: a problem upstream can deprive every later step, while a problem downstream may be invisible to a saturation probe.
学校氧级联从环境可用氧一路到细胞利用。它是因果图：上游故障可使后续缺氧，下游故障却可能在血氧探头上看不出来。

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:15.192
An obstructed airway limits entry. Pneumonia or edema can impair exchange. Hemorrhage and anemia reduce effective oxygen carriage, while poor cardiac output limits delivery of the oxygenated blood.
气道阻塞限制进入，肺炎或水肿损害交换，出血及贫血减少有效携氧，低心输出量限制已氧合血液的输送。

00:06:15.192 --> 00:06:30.144
Some toxic exposures impair cellular use, and sepsis can disturb several steps together. More oxygen concentration cannot by itself restore missing blood flow or make a poisoned cell use oxygen normally.
某些毒物损害细胞利用，脓毒症可同时干扰多个环节。单纯提高氧浓度，不能恢复缺失血流或让受毒细胞恢复正常利用。

00:06:30.144 --> 00:06:45.000
Name your evidence and uncertainty: poor ventilation, possible lung-exchange failure or possible shock. Multiple links may fail at once, so do not stop the assessment after finding the first abnormal sound.
应说明证据及不确定性：通气差、疑肺交换障碍或疑休克。多个环节可同时失效，不能找到第一个异常声音就停止评估。

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:59.112
Stridor suggests turbulent flow through a narrowed upper airway. Sudden onset during eating, progressive swelling and a traumatic neck injury create different pathways; the sound alone does not identify the cause.
喘鸣提示气流经狭窄上气道形成湍流。进食时突发、进行性肿胀、颈部创伤对应不同路径，声音本身不能判定原因。

00:06:59.112 --> 00:07:13.872
Snoring can accompany loss of pharyngeal tone; gurgling or wet sounds may indicate material needing appropriate clearance. Reassess after positioning, a manual maneuver or suction rather than assuming the airway is fixed.
鼾声可伴咽部张力丧失，咕噜或湿声可能提示需清除的物质。体位、手法或吸引后必须复查，不能假定气道已解决。

00:07:13.872 --> 00:07:28.920
Treat severe obstruction urgently with the applicable cause-specific procedure and help. Avoid repeated unnecessary stimulation or blind finger sweeps, and do not force a patient with a threatened airway into an intolerable position.
严重阻塞需按相应病因规程紧急处理并求援。避免反复无必要刺激及盲目手指探扫，不强迫濒危气道患者采取无法耐受体位。

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:42.840
A reduction in noise can mean better patency or less airflow. Confirm movement, air entry and patient function before declaring improvement; a silent obstructed patient may be deteriorating.
声音减轻既可能是更通畅，也可能是气流更少。应证实胸廓运动、进气及功能改善；阻塞后无声者可能在恶化。

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:56.640
Wheeze often reflects airflow through narrowed intrathoracic airways, but it is not an asthma certificate. History, exposure, fever, edema and other findings may support competing explanations.
哮鸣常反映气流通过狭窄胸内气道，但不等于哮喘确诊。病史、暴露、发热、水肿及其他发现可能支持不同解释。

00:07:56.640 --> 00:08:09.456
Observe the prolonged expiratory phase and whether the patient has time to empty the lungs. Increasing resistance and effort can progress to fatigue even while a saturation reading looks acceptable.
观察呼气是否延长、是否有足够排空时间。阻力及呼吸功增加可进展至疲劳，即使血氧读数看起来可接受。

00:08:09.456 --> 00:08:24.480
A silent chest in a severely breathless person may reflect very little airflow. Compare air entry, chest movement, speech and responsiveness; do not use disappearance of wheeze alone as a treatment endpoint.
严重气促者的“静默胸”可能意味着极少气流。应比较进气、胸廓运动、说话及反应，不能以哮鸣消失作为唯一治疗终点。

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:40.176
Provide the indicated authorized cause-specific therapy while supporting breathing. If spontaneous ventilation fails, move to effective assisted ventilation and escalation rather than repeating a previously chosen intervention indefinitely.
在支持呼吸的同时提供有适应证且获授权的病因治疗。自主通气失败时，应转为有效辅助通气及升级，而非无限重复原治疗。

00:08:40.176 --> 00:08:53.064
Crackles are discontinuous sounds associated with several processes, including fluid or reopening of small airways. Their presence helps form a pattern, not a unique diagnosis.
爆裂音是与多种过程相关的间断声音，包括液体或小气道重新开放。有助形成模式，但并非唯一诊断。

00:08:53.064 --> 00:09:08.736
An orthopneic patient with cardiac history and diffuse findings may have cardiogenic edema. Fever, cough and focal findings may suggest infection, but absence of fever does not exclude it and both conditions can coexist.
有心脏病史、端坐呼吸及弥漫发现者可能为心源性水肿；发热、咳嗽及局灶发现可能提示感染。但无发热不排除感染，两者也可并存。

00:09:08.736 --> 00:09:22.560
Assess pressure and perfusion before choosing a positive-pressure strategy. A patient who is alert and maintaining ventilation differs from one becoming hypotensive, exhausted or unable to protect the airway.
选择正压策略前先评估血压及灌注。清醒且维持通气者，与低血压、耗竭或无法保护气道者，处理不同。

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:35.472
CPAP can recruit alveoli and reduce work in suitable patients. It does not literally squeeze all water out of the lungs, treat every cause or remove the need for medication and repeated assessment.
适当患者使用 CPAP 可复张肺泡并减轻呼吸功，但不是把肺内水全部挤走，不能治疗所有病因，也不消除用药及复评需要。

00:09:35.472 --> 00:09:51.552
After trauma, inspect for asymmetry, wounds and abnormal movement, compare air entry and assess perfusion. A changing respiratory examination plus shock is more concerning than one uncertain auscultation finding.
创伤后检查不对称、伤口及异常运动，比较进气并评估灌注。呼吸检查持续变化并伴休克，比一个不确定听诊发现更令人担忧。

00:09:51.552 --> 00:10:03.552
Possible pneumothorax or other thoracic injury requires a time-critical cause-specific pathway. Do not delay escalation or transport while trying to prove a complete textbook triad.
疑气胸或其他胸部伤需要时间紧迫的病因路径。不要为了凑齐教科书三联征，延迟升级或转运。

00:10:03.552 --> 00:10:18.792
The school narrative mentions decompression as an advanced response. That is not an independent permission for every PCP student to perform it. Training, licence, employer authorization and the actual procedure determine who can act.
学校叙述提及减压作为高级反应，不等于每位 PCP 学生可独立实施。实际训练、执照、雇主授权及规程决定谁能操作。

00:10:18.792 --> 00:10:30.624
Suspected pneumothorax and traumatic respiratory distress also alter the safety of pressure support. Do not transfer a non-traumatic CPAP plan unchanged to this patient.
疑气胸及创伤性呼吸窘迫也改变正压支持的安全性。不能把非创伤 CPAP 计划原封不动用于此患者。

00:10:30.624 --> 00:10:45.744
For the school comparison exercise, retain its ninety-four to ninety-eight and eighty-eight to ninety-two target ranges. Current BCEHS A seven uses different operational wording; learn which source the question or clinical setting is using.
学校比较练习保留其百分之九十四至九十八及八十八至九十二目标。现行 BCEHS A07 的操作表述不同；要辨明题目或临床场景采用哪个来源。

00:10:45.744 --> 00:10:57.936
Titration means assessing the patient, delivering an appropriate concentration and rechecking response. A NEWS2 zero-point saturation band is not itself an oxygen prescription.
滴定意味着评估患者、给予适当浓度并重查反应。NEWS2 零分血氧区间本身不是氧疗处方。

00:10:57.936 --> 00:11:15.000
Do not explain oxygen-associated carbon-dioxide rise solely as switching off a hypoxic drive. Changes in ventilation-perfusion matching and carbon-dioxide carriage also matter. Controlled therapy is not a reason to abandon severe hypoxemia.
不能把氧相关二氧化碳上升仅解释为关闭“低氧驱动”。通气灌注匹配及二氧化碳携带改变也有关。控制氧疗不等于放任严重低氧。

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:29.904
If breathing is inadequate, oxygen alone cannot provide ventilation. Support the failing function and reassess consciousness, chest movement, oxygenation and carbon dioxide while following the applicable pathway.
呼吸不足时，单纯供氧无法提供通气。应支持失效功能，按适用途径复查意识、胸廓运动、氧合及二氧化碳。

00:11:29.904 --> 00:11:45.888
A low-flow nasal cannula allows speech and can support titrated oxygen, but the actual inspired concentration varies with breathing pattern, leaks and device flow. Do not convert a flow setting into a guaranteed inspired percentage.
低流量鼻导管便于说话及滴定，但实际吸入浓度随呼吸方式、漏气和流量改变。不能把流量设定等同保证的吸入百分比。

00:11:45.888 --> 00:12:00.192
A reservoir mask requires the appropriate manufacturer flow and a functioning reservoir, valves and seal. A poorly inflated reservoir or disconnected supply can make a reassuring mask appearance misleading.
储氧面罩需要制造商规定流量及正常储袋、阀门和贴合。储袋不充盈或供氧脱开时，外观戴着面罩也可能误导。

00:12:00.192 --> 00:12:14.088
No passive oxygen device compensates for an apneic patient. Open and clear the airway, provide effective ventilation when indicated, and choose another device only if it solves the actual remaining problem.
没有被动供氧器械能弥补呼吸暂停。应开放清理气道，按需有效通气，只在能解决实际剩余问题时选择其他器械。

00:12:14.088 --> 00:12:29.184
Estimate supply requirements for transport, including high oxygen consumption by some pressure devices. Recheck flow, connections and patient effect after movement, cylinder change and any unexpected deterioration.
应估计转运所需氧量，考虑某些正压器械耗氧较高。搬动、更换气瓶及任何意外恶化后，都复查流量、连接及患者效果。

00:12:29.184 --> 00:12:41.688
A capnogram displays exhaled carbon dioxide over time. First identify a repeatable respiratory waveform and a functioning sampling system before interpreting its end-tidal number.
二氧化碳图按时间显示呼出二氧化碳。解释呼气末数字前，先确认可重复呼吸波形及正常采样系统。

00:12:41.688 --> 00:12:56.544
Early expired conducting gas has little carbon dioxide, followed by the expiratory upstroke and alveolar plateau. The end-tidal value is measured near the end of that plateau; inspiration produces the descending limb.
早期呼出的传导气体含二氧化碳少，随后是呼气上升支及肺泡平台。呼气末值在平台末附近测得，吸气形成下降支。

00:12:56.544 --> 00:13:11.184
The school thirty-five to forty-five millimetre range is a reference, not a universal target for every condition. End-tidal and arterial carbon dioxide can diverge when dead space, perfusion or lung disease changes.
学校三十五至四十五毫米汞柱是参考，不是所有病况的统一目标。死腔、灌注或肺病改变时，呼气末与动脉二氧化碳可有差距。

00:13:11.184 --> 00:13:27.264
Use waveform shape, trend and examination together. A missing waveform can mean absent ventilation, disconnection, obstruction, displacement, low perfusion or sampling failure; assess and troubleshoot immediately.
波形形态、趋势及检查须合看。无波形可能是无通气、脱接、阻塞、移位、低灌注或采样故障，应立即评估排查。

00:13:27.264 --> 00:13:43.176
With reduced effective alveolar ventilation, carbon dioxide can accumulate and the end-tidal value may rise. A drowsy patient with shallow breaths and a rising trace needs functional breathing assessment, not simply oxygen adjustment.
有效肺泡通气下降时，二氧化碳可积聚，呼气末值可能升高。嗜睡、浅呼吸且数值上升者，需要功能性呼吸评估，而非只调氧。

00:13:43.176 --> 00:13:59.568
A falling value can follow improved ventilation, but can also indicate falling pulmonary blood flow. In a patient becoming pale and hypotensive, a lower end-tidal number may be a circulation warning rather than a respiratory success.
数值下降可随通气改善，也可反映肺血流下降。患者变苍白及低血压时，更低呼气末值可能是循环警报，而非呼吸成功。

00:13:59.568 --> 00:14:13.008
Obstructive disease may produce a sloping shark-fin pattern, but leaks, sampling and mixed disease affect the trace. A descriptive pattern supports reasoning; it does not replace the rest of the examination.
阻塞性疾病可出现倾斜鲨鱼鳍形，但漏气、采样及混合病变都会影响波形。描述性模式支持推理，不替代其他检查。

00:14:13.008 --> 00:14:26.976
Capnography often changes before pulse oximetry in hypoventilation, especially with oxygen therapy. There is no fixed universal thirty-to-sixty-second lag to memorize for every device and patient.
通气不足时，尤其吸氧下，二氧化碳监测常早于血氧变化。但不存在适用于所有设备和患者的固定三十至六十秒延迟。

00:14:26.976 --> 00:14:41.928
During resuscitation, pulmonary blood flow strongly influences exhaled carbon dioxide. Compression-generated flow is one contributor, but ventilation, the airway, metabolism and measurement also affect the number.
复苏时肺血流强烈影响呼出二氧化碳。按压产生的血流是因素之一，但通气、气道、代谢及测量同样影响数值。

00:14:41.928 --> 00:14:54.120
The school highlights ten and twenty millimetres as teaching markers. Do not convert them into a stand-alone pass-fail test for compressions or an independent rule to stop resuscitation.
学校把十和二十毫米汞柱作为教学标记。不能将其变成按压好坏的独立合格线，或独立终止复苏标准。

00:14:54.120 --> 00:15:07.848
An abrupt sustained rise can suggest improved circulation or return of spontaneous circulation. Correlate it with the appropriate clinical and rhythm assessment without creating unnecessary compression interruptions.
突然持续上升可能提示循环改善或自主循环恢复。应以适当临床及心律评估核实，不制造不必要按压中断。

00:15:07.848 --> 00:15:20.832
If the value falls unexpectedly, verify the patient and airway circuit and review ventilation and compression quality. Treat the cause, not a target number detached from the resuscitation context.
数值意外下降时，应核查患者及气道回路，并复查通气及按压质量。处理原因，而非追逐脱离复苏背景的数字。

00:15:20.832 --> 00:15:35.952
A bag can be squeezed while no effective volume reaches the lungs. Check the equipment, position, airway patency and mask seal before increasing force. Use an airway adjunct when indicated and compatible with the patient.
球囊可以被挤压，却没有有效气量到肺。加力前先查器械、体位、通畅及贴合；按适应证及耐受情况使用辅助气道。

00:15:35.952 --> 00:15:49.800
Where two providers are available, one maintains the airway and two-handed mask seal while the other gives breaths and watches the chest. Lift the jaw toward the mask rather than pressing the mask hard into soft tissue.
有两人时，一人维持气道及双手密封，另一人送气并观察胸部。应将下颌提向面罩，而非把面罩硬压进软组织。

00:15:49.800 --> 00:16:04.608
Deliver only enough volume for a slight definite chest rise, allow exhalation and monitor effectiveness. Excess volume, pressure or rate can inflate the stomach, increase aspiration risk and impair circulation.
只送到轻微而明确胸起，留出呼气时间并监测有效性。过量容积、压力或频率可致胃充气、增加误吸风险并损害循环。

00:16:04.608 --> 00:16:18.816
If the chest does not rise, correct patency and seal, inspect for obstruction and equipment problems, and escalate the airway plan if needed. Repeated failed squeezes do not count as successful ventilation.
胸部不起时，应纠正通畅及密封，检查阻塞和器械问题，必要时升级气道计划。反复无效挤球不算成功通气。

00:16:18.816 --> 00:16:34.536
The school gives ten to twelve adult breaths per minute as general BVM teaching. The named twenty-twenty-five AHA adult respiratory-arrest branch, with a definite pulse, specifies one breath every six seconds, or ten per minute.
学校一般 BVM 教学给成人每分钟十至十二次。明确有脉搏的二零二五 AHA 成人呼吸停止分支，规定每六秒一次，即每分钟十次。

00:16:34.536 --> 00:16:50.088
For the latter branch, use visible chest rise and reassess pulse every two minutes. A patient without a definite pulse and without an advanced airway follows the compression-and-breath sequence, not uninterrupted rescue breaths alone.
该分支以可见胸起为准，每两分钟复查脉搏。无明确脉搏且无高级气道者应走按压与通气序列，而非只连续人工呼吸。

00:16:50.088 --> 00:17:04.320
These numbers are not an instruction to ignore spontaneous breaths or force a single rate in every illness. Coordinate assisted breaths appropriately and allow exhalation, especially with obstructive physiology.
这些数字不要求忽略自主呼吸或所有病症强用一个频率。应适当同步辅助呼吸并留出呼气，尤其存在阻塞生理时。

00:17:04.320 --> 00:17:19.296
Pediatric rates, advanced-airway CPR and the specific PEEP procedure have separate instructions. State the patient and branch before quoting a rate, and use the current school resuscitation standard for its supervised skills check.
儿科频率、高级气道 CPR 及特定 PEEP 规程另有指令。报频率前先说患者及分支；学校督导技能检查采用其当前复苏标准。

00:17:19.296 --> 00:17:33.168
PEEP retains pressure at the end of expiration. CPAP provides continuous pressure during spontaneous breathing. Neither name guarantees effective ventilation or eliminates the need to examine airway integrity.
PEEP 在呼气末保留压力，CPAP 在自主呼吸全程提供持续压力。两者名称都不保证有效通气，也不取消气道完整性检查。

00:17:33.168 --> 00:17:49.968
Current PR ten starts indicated BVM PEEP at five centimetres of water, with monitored adjustments of two point five up to ten. The procedure has specific exclusions and requires consultation for persistent hypoxemia despite maximal therapy.
现行 PR10 对有适应证的 BVM PEEP 从五厘米水柱开始，在监测下每次加二点五，最多十。规程有明确排除项，最大治疗后仍低氧需会诊。

00:17:49.968 --> 00:18:06.096
That procedure excludes cardiac arrest, traumatic respiratory arrest, suspected pneumothorax and defined low-pressure states. Its usual eight-to-ten breath wording is context-specific, not a reason to overwrite every other ventilation algorithm.
该规程排除心搏骤停、创伤性呼吸停止、疑气胸及规定低血压状态。其通常每分钟八至十次的说法针对该情境，不能覆盖其他通气算法。

00:18:06.096 --> 00:18:21.720
Monitor pressure, chest mechanics and oxygenation, and discontinue when a contraindication or equipment concern develops. Pressure is a treatment with physiological trade-offs, not an automatic upgrade for every breathless patient.
监测血压、胸部力学及氧合，出现禁忌或器械问题时停止。正压有生理代价，并非所有气促者的自动升级。

00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:34.368
CPAP helps a suitable spontaneously breathing patient; it does not generate mandatory breaths. The most important first question is whether the person can maintain the airway and keep ventilating.
CPAP 帮助适合的自主呼吸患者，不会产生强制呼吸。首要问题是能否维持气道并继续有效通气。

00:18:34.368 --> 00:18:47.352
For the current PR nine selection exercise, check the listed age, distress findings and supplemental-oxygen context together. An isolated low room-air saturation is not the whole indication.
按现行 PR09 做选择练习时，应一起核查年龄、窘迫发现及已吸氧背景。孤立室内空气低血氧不是完整适应证。

00:18:47.352 --> 00:18:58.392
Authorization and training are part of the decision, not a separate administrative detail. A lecture about CPAP cannot authorize a learner to apply it independently.
授权及训练本身就是决策部分，不是无关行政细节。读完 CPAP 讲义不能授权学习者独立使用。

00:18:58.392 --> 00:19:10.608
Explain the aim, obtain applicable consent and plan what you will do if it fails before fitting the device. The patient must be able to report intolerance and cooperate with close reassessment.
佩戴前解释目标、取得适用同意，并先计划失败如何处理。患者需能表达不耐受，配合密切复评。

00:19:10.608 --> 00:19:24.744
In the public PR nine procedure, the listed exclusions must be checked before treatment and again if the condition changes. Failure to follow commands is not just a comfort problem; it undermines safe use.
现行公开 PR09 的排除项须在治疗前检查，病情改变后再查。无法遵从指令不只是舒适问题，而会破坏安全使用前提。

00:19:24.744 --> 00:19:38.544
A patient with slower shallow breaths and falling consciousness needs effective ventilation, not a tighter CPAP strap. Remove an ineffective or unsafe strategy and enact the prepared airway-support plan.
呼吸变慢浅且意识下降者，需要有效通气，而不是把 CPAP 带绑更紧。应停止无效或不安全策略，实施预备气道支持计划。

00:19:38.544 --> 00:19:51.432
Vomiting or inability to protect the airway creates an aspiration concern. Anticipate access to suction and an alternate support method rather than waiting until secretions cannot be cleared.
呕吐或无法保护气道带来误吸风险。应预备吸引及替代支持方法，不能等到分泌物无法清除才应对。

00:19:51.432 --> 00:20:04.944
Use the full examination to distinguish anxiety with maintained function from evolving failure. Reassurance can improve tolerance, but it must not be used to explain away physiological deterioration.
应以完整检查区分功能维持的焦虑与正在发生的衰竭。安抚可改善耐受，但不能拿焦虑解释掉生理恶化。

00:20:04.944 --> 00:20:17.736
The PR nine fixed-flow device starts at five litres per minute if possible, otherwise six. That is a device-linked setup, not a universal conversion between litres per minute and centimetres of water.
PR09 的定流量器械尽可能从每分钟五升开始，否则六升。这是具体器械设置，不是升每分钟与厘米水柱的通用换算。

00:20:17.736 --> 00:20:34.248
Let the patient hold the mask initially and build the seal progressively with explanation. Once tolerated, secure it and recheck leaks and effect; follow the manufacturer chart, never exceeding ten centimetres of water under PR nine.
起初让患者自己持面罩，一边解释一边逐步密封。耐受后固定，复查漏气及效果；依制造商表调整，PR09 下不得超过十厘米水柱。

00:20:34.248 --> 00:20:48.480
Do not attach a BVM to a CPAP mask as a substitute circuit, and do not delay indicated medication to fit it. Equipment-specific nebulizer connections and oxygen changes require the actual device procedure.
不能把 BVM 接到 CPAP 面罩当替代回路，也不能为佩戴而延误有适应证药物。雾化连接及氧流改变必须依实际器械规程。

00:20:48.480 --> 00:21:06.696
Reassess the whole patient after application and each change: effort, volume, mental state, oxygenation and circulation. A brief initial saturation change needs interpretation, but ongoing deterioration requires action, not passive waiting.
佩戴及每次调整后复评全人：用力、气量、意识、氧合及循环。初始短暂血氧变化需解释，但持续恶化必须行动，不能被动等待。

00:21:06.696 --> 00:21:21.720
In this new simulation, an initially distressed adult becomes quieter during treatment. The oxygen saturation remains ninety-five percent on supplemental oxygen, but the patient is drowsier and moving much less air.
本原创模拟中，最初窘迫的成人治疗中变安静。吸氧下血氧仍为百分之九十五，但更嗜睡、气流明显减少。

00:21:21.720 --> 00:21:35.760
The correct explanation is not that the wheeze and rate improved. The combined fall in responsiveness, rate and tidal movement indicates loss of effective ventilation; carbon-dioxide rise supports that concern.
不能解释为哮鸣及频率已改善。反应、频率及潮气运动同时下降，提示有效通气丧失，二氧化碳上升支持这一担忧。

00:21:35.760 --> 00:21:48.912
Return to airway and breathing support, obtain additional help and use effective assisted ventilation within the applicable pathway. Preserve enough expiratory time and reassess for pressure-related harm.
应返回气道及呼吸支持、增援，并按适用途径进行有效辅助通气。保留足够呼气时间，复查正压相关损害。

00:21:48.912 --> 00:22:01.608
State what changed, what you did and what happened next. That explanation demonstrates recognition of a transition from distress to failure; listing a bronchodilator name alone does not.
应说清变化、行动及后续反应。这才展示识别从窘迫到衰竭的转变；只列支气管扩张药名不够。

00:22:01.608 --> 00:22:16.488
An adult with the displayed initial findings may satisfy the physiological PR nine criteria, but that is only after checking the rest of the history, examination and exclusions. The case is original, not a school assessment answer.
显示初始发现的成人，可能满足 PR09 生理标准，但须先核查其他病史、检查及排除项。此案例原创，不是学校考核答案。

00:22:16.488 --> 00:22:30.720
A trained authorized provider could select CPAP with close monitoring and appropriate concurrent care. Predict an improvement in work, oxygenation and maintained mentation rather than claiming the device cures the underlying disease.
受训获授权人员可选择 CPAP，密切监测并提供并行照护。预期呼吸功、氧合改善且意识保持，而非宣称器械治愈基础病。

00:22:30.720 --> 00:22:45.384
Now change one variable group: the patient becomes drowsy with eight shallow breaths per minute. The treatment assumptions fail. This is a ventilation and airway-support problem even if a saturation has not yet fallen.
现在改变一组功能变量：患者嗜睡，每分钟八次浅呼吸。治疗前提已失效，即使血氧尚未下降，也已是通气及气道支持问题。

00:22:45.384 --> 00:22:58.464
Stop treating the original indication as permanent. Reassess immediately, provide the indicated alternate support and escalate resources, communicating the deterioration and actual response.
原有适应证并不永久成立。应立即复评，提供有适应证替代支持并升级资源，报告恶化及真实反应。

00:22:58.464 --> 00:23:13.680
An unresponsive adult has five shallow breaths per minute, a definite pulse and a high saturation while receiving oxygen. Possible opioid exposure is relevant, but the decisive initial finding is inadequate ventilation.
无反应成人每分钟五次浅呼吸，有明确脉搏，吸氧下血氧高。可能阿片暴露有意义，但首个决定性发现是通气不足。

00:23:13.680 --> 00:23:24.504
Open and clear the airway and provide effective assisted breaths. Waiting for the saturation to fall or for naloxone to work leaves a failing function unsupported.
应开放清理气道，提供有效辅助呼吸。等待血氧下降或纳洛酮起效，会使失效功能一直没有支持。

00:23:24.504 --> 00:23:37.128
Give naloxone when indicated and authorized, using the actual route and schedule taught in the medication lesson. The aim is adequate breathing, not forcing complete wakefulness at any cost.
有适应证及授权时，按药物课所教实际途径与序列给纳洛酮。目标是充分呼吸，而非不计代价完全叫醒。

00:23:37.128 --> 00:23:52.584
Reassess sustained breathing, circulation and other possible causes. Recurrent depression can occur after an initial response; a transient improvement is not permission to end monitoring or make an unsupported non-conveyance decision.
应复查呼吸能否持续、循环及其他可能病因。初次反应后可再次抑制，暂时改善不等于可结束监测或无依据决定不转运。

00:23:52.584 --> 00:24:05.304
Record what was happening before the intervention and the support already in place. A saturation without oxygen-device context and a respiratory rate without depth lose important meaning.
记录干预前状态及已有支持。血氧缺少供氧器械背景、频率缺少深度信息，都丢失重要意义。

00:24:05.304 --> 00:24:21.096
Compare work, speech, chest movement, air entry, mental state, perfusion, saturation and appropriate waveform trends. Improvement should be coherent across relevant findings, not merely one selected number.
比较呼吸功、说话、胸动、进气、意识、灌注、血氧及适当波形趋势。改善应在相关发现间一致，而非只挑一个数字。

00:24:21.096 --> 00:24:34.968
An unexpected response should reopen the differential and the equipment check. Consider disease progression, an incorrect assumption, a leak, obstruction, depleted oxygen or a pressure-related adverse effect.
反应意外时应重开鉴别及器械检查。考虑病情发展、原假设错误、漏气、阻塞、氧气耗尽或正压不良影响。

00:24:34.968 --> 00:24:50.376
Handover must include baseline, change, device or medication details and remaining concern. Saying respiratory patient, better after oxygen hides the reasoning and may obscure ongoing ventilatory failure.
交接应包括基线、变化、器械或药物细节及剩余担忧。只说“呼吸患者，吸氧后好转”会掩盖推理，也可能遮住持续通气失败。

00:24:50.376 --> 00:25:04.032
In the school station, state your role and identify the immediate respiratory problem before choosing a device. Prepare the equipment and a fallback, and assign a second provider when the skill benefits from one.
学校站点中，先说明角色及即时呼吸问题，再选器械。准备设备及后备方案，需要两人的技能应安排第二人。

00:25:04.032 --> 00:25:17.928
Demonstrate a patent airway and effective bag-mask technique on the appropriate trainer. Then explain how you distinguish an alert, spontaneously ventilating CPAP candidate from a patient needing assisted ventilation.
在适当模拟器展示气道通畅及有效球囊面罩技术，然后解释如何区分清醒自主通气的 CPAP 候选者，与需要辅助通气者。

00:25:17.928 --> 00:25:32.856
Have the observer change one feature: a leak, weaker breathing, a falling pressure or a disconnected sampling line. State the finding, correct the cause and verify the actual effect rather than announcing the skill complete.
让观察者改变一个特征：漏气、呼吸变弱、血压下降或采样线脱开。说出发现、纠正原因并验证实际效果，而非直接宣布完成。

00:25:32.856 --> 00:25:47.016
Use the original practice questions and paired reading to explain the decisions without notes. Physical competence, patient safety and the school skills sign-off still require supervised demonstration, not playback completion.
用原创练习及对照阅读，脱稿解释决策。操作能力、患者安全及学校技能签核仍需要督导展示，不以播放完成代替。
